  "notes": "GAAP statements (modified accrual governmental funds, accrual proprietary funds), as FY2023/FY2024. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p6); business-type from the proprietary funds statement Total Funds column (p10). 'Taxes' 93,713 is property tax per the Statement of Activities general revenue line (p4). Proceeds from sale of assets 964 (other financing sources, p6) recorded as other_financing. Only supplementary schedule is a combined all-funds budgetary comparison (cash basis, p13), so as in FY2023/FY2024 detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p6) and proprietary funds (p9-10) statements; the combined schedule lines are not recorded. Capital outlay on the statement mixes General and Street Fund columns, so it is labelled plain 'Capital outlay'. ending_cash = cash + cash with county treasurer from the governmental funds balance sheet (restricted cash 201,702 excluded, as FY2023); no beginning cash printed. Balance sheet 'Due to other funds' line (internal balances 144,482 / (144,482)) recorded as printed. Read pages 1-13 of 13."
